Let's plug $\blueD{y=-2}$, $\maroonD{x=3}$, and $\goldD{\dfrac{dy}{dt}=2.1}$ into the equation we obtained:

$\begin{align}
2\blueD{y}\cdot\goldD{\dfrac{dy}{dt}}&=2\maroonD{x}\cdot\dfrac{dx}{dt}
\\\\
2(\blueD{-2})\cdot\goldD{2.1}&=2(\maroonD{3})\cdot\dfrac{dx}{dt}
\\\\
-8.4&=6\cdot \dfrac{dx}{dt}
\\\\
-1.4&=\dfrac{dx}{dt}
\end{align}$
